works: Whatever {N} chose, the chicks fly, and the marsh {N} let flood ten years ago is a place people speak of.
fails: The nest fails in a wet week early in the summer, as first nests often do, and the cranes leave.
fails: The fuss fades after a season, the cranes move on, and {N} goes back to the ordinary counts and the ordinary weeks.

# ================================================================ world-only (magic)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 9. the circle meets at the old stones (only: magic; pairs D1b)
# The magic crossing to the summit (worlds-land.py, WORLD_ONLY_LAND): at midsummer the druids of every grove gather at
# the old stones to name a new archdruid. For a druid of the grove ([steward of the land]) of three years or more
# (LIFE_LAND), each one-colour way is a try for [keeper of the land] (archdruid of the circle) at its real chance, 6.
# Blue's way takes up the old pact written in the circle's oldest book, with the spirits of the deep grove: their power,
# never the druid's own gift, at 15, with the price on a closed: approval: line and its backfire (seven winters keeping
# the deep grove's bounds by night, and the circle learns of it). The pairs are the honest ways: the moor's springs
# tended with the young druids, the pact's past takers named before the circle, the oldest book read through the night,
# the druid of the high moors spoken for, and every grove walked first. They form a ring (each colour in two), so their
# chances are solved around the singles (66 and 84) until every colour's mean is 40.5. per_year as the other roads'
# world-only events; LIFE_LAND gates it (three years a druid of the grove).

== the circle meets at the old stones
tier: life event
only: magic
stages: adult mature elder
age: 35-100
holds: steward of the land
tenure: 3-99
per_year: 0 0 0 .02 .02 .01
drivers: fortune+.2 community+.1
times: per druid of the grove of three years or more in the magic world a year: about 1 in 60 is at the old stones when the circle gathers to name a new archdruid (estimate); in many old tales the keepers of the woods chose their chief at a gathering, and some said the spirits of the deep woods had a voice in it (estimate); about 1 life in 1,000 is a druid of the grove (catalogue share)
likelier: an old archdruid failing, a druid known for the grove kept, a midsummer feast, a circle already divided
rarer: a young archdruid in good health, a grove far from the stones, a druid the circle mistrusts
gap: 8-20
domain: community.5
tone: mixed
life: community, nature
horizon: months
roles: elder, rival, mentor, colleague
magic: the druids of every grove gather at the old stones to name a new archdruid, and the spirits of the deep grove offer an old pact
scene magic: At midsummer the druids of every grove in the realm walk to the old stones on the high moor, where the archdruids have been named for longer than the books remember. {elder}, the old archdruid, is too frail to keep the circle, and will step down at the next full moon. On the first night a voice comes to {N} out of the deep grove beyond the stones: the old spirits of the woods will win the circle for {N}, if {N} takes up the old pact and pays the price they will name. {rival}, it is whispered, has heard the same voice.
scene magic W: The circle names its archdruid by its own law: a voice from every grove, and the eldest's word last. {N} is uneasy at anything that comes round the side of it.
scene magic U: The old pact is written in the circle's oldest book, in a hand nobody has read for a hundred years. {N} knows where the book is kept, and how to read the hand.
scene magic B: The druid of the high moors has more groves behind him than anyone, and no wish to be archdruid himself. {N} knows what his word would be worth.
scene magic R: The stones hum at night, and the deep grove beyond them is dark and full of sound. {N} wants to walk into it alone and see what is there.
scene magic G: Every grove of the realm has its own woods, its own springs and its own seasons. {N} would like to have walked them all before asking any of them for a voice.
- W | wait for the circle's naming, and stand by its law of choosing | v: conformity, tradition | identity | title: keeper of the land | chance: 6
- U | take up the old pact from the circle's oldest book, at the price the spirits name | v: achievement, power | title: keeper of the land | mark: hid a wrong | closed: approval: the spirits' pact, kept from the circle; backfire: the price comes due: seven winters keeping the deep grove's bounds by night, and the circle learns of the pact | self_control: - | chance: 15
- B | count the groves one by one, and win the waverers before the naming | v: power, achievement | title: keeper of the land | chance: 6
- R | walk alone into the deep grove at night, and ask the voice its name | v: stimulation, self-direction | title: keeper of the land | mark: took a wild risk | chance: 6
- G | go on keeping your own grove, and leave the naming to its season | v: tradition, benevolence | title: keeper of the land | chance: 6
- RG | tend the springs of the high moor with the young druids every night until the naming | v: stimulation, tradition | habit | foot: place prod.wild | chance: 84
- UB | find out who took up the old pact before, and name them before the circle | v: achievement, security | mark: made an enemy | chance: 66
- UR | read the circle's oldest book through the night, and learn what the pact truly asks | v: achievement, stimulation | mark: learned a skill | chance: 66
- WB | speak for the druid of the high moors, and stand at his right hand | v: security, benevolence | door | grants: friend in power | chance: 84
- WG | walk to every grove of the realm first, and ask each for its voice | v: tradition, conformity | foot: means time-.05 | chance: 66
works: At the full moon the circle names its archdruid, the horns sound across the moor, and the groves settle into the new years.
works: Whatever {N} chose, the midsummer gathering ends in peace, and the druids go home to their woods.
fails: The circle names {rival}, and nobody speaks of the voice in the deep grove again.
fails: The gathering splits over the naming, it drags on for a year, and {N} is left out of the end of it.
